Thai character names: stop trimming CP874 bytes as whitespace.

TRIM_CHARS contains \255 (octal) = 0xAD, which is the Thai letter ญ (YO YING) in CP874/TIS-620,
and 0xA0 (NBSP). normalize_name() replaces runs of these with a space and trims them from the ends,
so any name containing ญ is corrupted on character creation and rename (rathena#6157). This is the
change of upstream PR #9990, closed unmerged on 2026-05-30. Applied by services/rathena/Dockerfile
with --fuzz=0 against the pinned RATHENA_REF.

--- a/src/char/char.hpp
+++ b/src/char/char.hpp
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@
 	bool char_rename_guild;	// Character renaming in a guild
 };
 
-#define TRIM_CHARS "\255\xA0\032\t\x0A\x0D " //The following characters are trimmed regardless because they cause confusion and problems on the servers. [Skotlex]
+#define TRIM_CHARS "\032\t\x0A\x0D " //The following characters are trimmed regardless because they cause confusion and problems on the servers. [Skotlex]
 struct CharServ_Config {
 	char userid[24];
 	char passwd[24];
